  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Interpeace Rwanda 2021-25</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Interpeace Rwanda 2021-25</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Interpeace har ans&#xf6;kt om 77 miljoner SEK i st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra insatsen &apos;&#x2019;Reinforcing community capacity for social cohesion and reconciliation through Societal Trauma Healing in Rwanda&#x2019;, 2021-2025, mellan juli 2021 till juni 2022.  Insatsen genomf&#xf6;rs i samarbete med Prison Fellowship Rwanda (RFP), Haguruka och Dignity in Detention Organisation (DiDe). 

Insatsens m&#xe5;l syftar till att st&#xe4;rka den mentala h&#xe4;lsan hos de som drabbats av folkmordet mot Tutsierna 1994 och deras emotionella och finansiella resiliens och i l&#xe4;ngde verka f&#xf6;r h&#xe5;llbar fred. Mer specifikt syftar insatsen p&#xe5; att st&#xe4;rka &#xe5;terintegreringen av f&#xe4;ngelsf&#xe5;ngar d&#xf6;mda f&#xf6;r folkmordsbrott som kommer att sl&#xe4;ppas under de kommande fyra &#xe5;ren och minska risker relaterad till &#xe5;terintegreringen, s&#xe5;som f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade &#xf6;kade fall av k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld, sp&#xe4;nningar, konflikter och &#xf6;kade niv&#xe5;er av trauma. Insatsen arbetar &#xe4;ven mer Rwandas yngre befolkning f&#xf6;r att minska intergenerationstrauma och d&#xe4;rmed motverka radikalisering och &#xf6;kade sp&#xe4;nningar bland den yngre generationen. Programmet &#xe4;r uppdelat i fyra resultatomr&#xe5;den med specifika m&#xe5;l och aktiviteter, (1) F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad l&#xe4;kning och psykosocial motst&#xe5;ndskraft bland m&#xe4;n, kvinnor och unga i samh&#xe4;llet och inom f&#xe4;ngelser, (2) F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad social sammanh&#xe5;llning och &#xe5;terintegrering av folkmordsd&#xf6;mda f&#xe4;ngelseg&#xe5;ngar (3) Inkluderande och kollektiva f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjningsm&#xf6;jligheter f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;n, kvinnor och unga i samh&#xe4;llet och f&#xe4;ngelser f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra v&#xe4;lbefinnandet, social samanh&#xe5;llning och f&#xf6;rsoning, och (4) St&#xe4;rkande av nationell policy och program inom ramen f&#xf6;r helande, social sammanh&#xe5;llning och f&#xf6;rsoning, samt f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjningsm&#xf6;jligheter f&#xf6;r de fattigaste, inklusive sl&#xe4;ppta f&#xe4;ngelsef&#xe5;ngar och de som &#xf6;verlevde folkmordet mot Tutsierna.  

Sverige st&#xe5;r som enskild finansi&#xe4;r av insatsen men f&#xf6;rhoppningen &#xe4;r antalet givare kommer att &#xf6;ka under insatsens g&#xe5;ng vid en eventuell ut&#xf6;kning av insatser till andra distrikt. CKCK MSK kommer vidaref&#xf6;rmedlas till partnerorganisationer samt TVET-institutioner.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Interpeace has submitted to the Embassy a proposal for a four-year programme titled, &#x2019;Reinforcing community capacity for social cohesion and reconciliation through Societal Trauma Healing in Rwanda&#x2019;. The proposed duration of the programme is July 2021 to June 2025, and the budget is 77&#xa0;million SEK. The contribution will be implemented in close collaboration with Prison Fellowship Rwanda ( RFP), HAGURUKA and Dignity in Detention Organization (DiDe).

The proposed programme aims to address and heal the psycho-social wounds that has been caused by the 1994 Genocide against the Tutsi and strengthen social cohesion, trust building and socio-economic development with the longer perspective of promoting sustainable peace in Rwanda. This will be achieved through trauma healing, community dialogue, and small-scale livelihood projects. A strong emphasis is put on the releases of prisoners convicted of crimes relating to the Genocide against the Tutsi and their reintegration back into their communities as well as on youth, and their ability to heal from inter-generational trauma. The program is divided into four result areas with specific goals and activities, (1) Improved healing and psychosocial resilience among men, women and young people in society and in prisons, (2) Improved social cohesion and reintegration of genocidal convictions (3) Inclusion and collective livelihoods for men, women and young people in society and prisons for the development of well-being, social cohesion and reconciliation; genocide survivor.

Sweden is the sole financier of the contribution, but there is an anticipation that additional donors will fund a potential up-scale of the programme. CKCK MSK will be passed on to partner organizations and TVET institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the programme is to strengthen psychosocial and socioeconomic resilience for sustainable peace among communities in five districts in Rwanda through five outcomes:

Enhanced healing and psychosocial resilience among men, women, youth and other
vulnerable groups in communities and prisons.

Enhanced social cohesion and prisoners psychosocial reintegration.

Improved socio-economic inclusion and collective livelihood opportunities for men,
women, youth, and other vulnerable groups.

National policies and programmes on healing, social cohesion and collective livelihoods
are informed by lessons learned from programme interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
